---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "May 6, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Wake Rower — Privacy Policy"
  description="Wake Rower privacy policy. No accounts, fully offline, no trackers."
  noindex
>
  <main class="min-h-screen px-6 md:px-24 lg:px-32 max-w-3xl mx-auto py-20 md:py-32">
    <a
      href="/"
      class="inline-block font-mono text-xs text-title-dark hover:text-primary transition-colors mb-12"
    >
      ← rafaelmendes.dev
    </a>

    <p class="text-primary font-mono text-sm mb-4">Wake Rower</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-title-light mb-4">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="text-title-dark font-mono text-xs mb-12">
      Last updated: {lastUpdated}
    </p>

    <section class="border-l-2 border-primary bg-card/40 px-6 py-5 mb-16">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-primary mb-3">tl;dr</p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-title-light">
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="text-primary font-mono">▸</span>
          <span>No accounts. Nothing to sign up for.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="text-primary font-mono">▸</span>
          <span>Fully offline. The app never talks to a server.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="text-primary font-mono">▸</span>
          <span>No trackers, no analytics, no ads, no third parties.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="text-primary font-mono">▸</span>
          <span>Your workouts stay on your device. Always.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <div class="space-y-12 text-title-dark leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-title-light mb-3">
          What data we collect
        </h2>
        <p>
          None. Wake Rower does not collect, transmit, or receive any personal
          data. There is no signup, no login, no email, no profile.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-title-light mb-3">
          Where your workouts are stored
        </h2>
        <p>
          Locally on your device, in the app's private storage. Workouts never
          leave your phone unless you explicitly export them yourself.
          Uninstalling the app deletes everything.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-title-light mb-3">
          Network access
        </h2>
        <p>
          Wake Rower does not make network requests. The app works fully offline
          and has no backend. You can put your phone in airplane mode and
          nothing will change.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-title-light mb-3">
          Analytics and trackers
        </h2>
        <p>
          There are none. No Google Analytics, no Firebase, no Sentry, no
          crash reporting, no ad SDKs, no fingerprinting. The app contains
          zero third-party SDKs of that kind.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-title-light mb-3">
          Permissions the app requests
        </h2>
        <p>
          Only what's needed to run a workout. Optional access to motion
          sensors and Bluetooth (to connect to a rower) is requested at the
          moment you choose to use those features, and never sent anywhere.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-title-light mb-3">
          Children's privacy
        </h2>
        <p>
          Because Wake Rower collects no data at all, it collects none from
          children either.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-title-light mb-3">
          Changes to this policy
        </h2>
        <p>
          If the app ever changes in a way that affects privacy, this page
          will be updated and the date at the top will reflect the change.
          The current commitment — no accounts, fully offline, no trackers —
          is the whole point of the app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-title-light mb-3">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions?
          <a
            href="mailto:rdesignedhead@gmail.com"
            class="text-primary hover:underline"
          >
            rdesignedhead@gmail.com
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <footer class="mt-20 pt-8 border-t border-title-dark/20">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-title-dark">
        Wake Rower — built by Rafael Mendes.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>
